From 59859088e88079a4156815877e2bd0de112be8e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Popa <elena.popa@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Oct 2025 13:14:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] imx9:soc: remove the ft_add_optee_node call from SPL

When U-Boot proper is skipped, the ft_system_setup() function must be
called in SPL. This function calls, in turn, the ft_add_optee_node(),
which will not execute correctly, because at that point, rom_pointer is
not initialized with the correct values.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific Falcon Mode support]

Signed-off-by: Elena Popa <elena.popa@nxp.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/soc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/soc.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/soc.c
index 30ad5d4dc22..8b579390832 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/soc.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/soc.c
@@ -846,7 +846,11 @@ int ft_system_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
 		disable_lpm(blob);
 	}
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD)
+	return 0;
+#else
 	return ft_add_optee_node(blob, bd);
+#endif
 }
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_ENV_VARS_UBOOT_RUNTIME_CONFIG)
-- 
2.34.1

